  {
    "path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r88/discovery.md",
    "lines": [
      "1. Amdeberhan\u2013Koutschan\u2013Zeilberger, *A tale of Toeplitz plus Hankel determinants*, author PDF https://sites.math.rutgers.edu/~zeilberg/mamarim/mamarimPDF/tem2.pdf. Conjecture1 gives a product for det T_{n,m}(x), T_ij=binom(x+m,j-i+m)-binom(x+m,m-i-j-1). Read the actual Theorem2.1 condensation proof, Corollary2.2 substitution and Theorem3.1 constant-term proof through its final common integrand. The latter identifies det T with det B and explicitly proves Conjecture1. Rejected before new proof investment. The final q-analogue question is not a precisely specified formula and is not selected."
    ]
  },
  {
    "path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/kinetic-contribution-r1/review.md",
    "lines": [
      "Catalogue item 364 in `sources/CONTENTS.md` pairs H with the stable-radial-potential law of large numbers. That companion derives `L^1` convergence of factorial marginals for a different force law. Catalogue item 363 is nonuniqueness for the Boltzmann equation. Quantum hard-sphere condensation titles in the same catalogue are different models. H's own introduction is the fluctuation statement in this pin. A line search of `CONTENTS.md` for process-convergence wording returned no kinetic path theorem."
    ]
  },
  {
    "path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/arithmetic-r162aj-contribution-r1/private/REVIEW.md",
    "lines": [
      "The ordinary parity-rank conversion used in HS gives the universal graph on these leaves. In a finite even edge-labeled graph, ranks at the odd priorities in descending order are nonincreasing on the corresponding truncated lexicographic tuples, strictly decreasing on an odd edge at that priority. Such ranks are obtained by successively removing the highest even edges and ranking the acyclic condensation across the highest odd edges; a highest odd edge cannot lie on a cycle. There are at most N distinct leaf ranks. Embed their ordered rank tree in U. Put an edge between universal leaves whenever the appropriate truncated comparison holds (strict for odd, non-strict for even). This graph is even: an infinite path with highest recurrent priority odd would eventually have a finite rank prefix decrease strictly infinitely often. It receives the rank homomorphism from every even graph of size at most N. Thus its entire adjacency relation can be generated by comparisons of finite navigation strings, at cost polynomial in its own size, q and string length. This supplies the finite-bit construction detail behind the universal-graph oracle; no nonuniform lookup or unread faster graph oracle is needed."
    ]
  },
  {
    "path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/structural-r198-contribution-r1/packet/authored/REVIEW.md",
    "lines": [
